# `**/`: a bare `node_modules` or `dist` only matches at the context root, so the workspaces'
# host node_modules and build output were sent as context, and the Dockerfiles' `COPY shared/`,
# `backend/`, `frontend/` (after `npm ci`, before the build) laid them over the image's install.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
# Generated from the locale sources by copy-locales.cjs, which `npm run build` runs as prebuild
# inside the images.
frontend/public/locales
backend/locales
data
# The dev stack's data dir, the counterpart to `data/` above. Without this the whole dev MariaDB
# and Redis state is sent as build context, and once the dev stack has run the build fails
# outright: docker-compose.dev.yml's db/redis bind mounts are owned by uid 999, which the build
# context sender cannot read. .gitignore already excludes it. (audit DEV-STACK-ISOLATION-1)
data-dev
.git
.env
*.md
tests
**/coverage
.nyc_output
# The docs tour and its screenshots are not part of any image (docs/*.md are, for the in-game Help).
e2e
docs/screenshots
